## index.ts

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { loadConfig } from "./config";
import { WebAppStack } from "./components/web-app-stack";

const env = loadConfig();
const cfg = new pulumi.Config();

// Secret: encrypted via Pulumi config (`pulumi config set --secret dbPassword`)
const dbPassword = cfg.requireSecret("dbPassword");

new WebAppStack("webapp", { env, dbPassword });
```

## Pulumi.dev.yaml

```yaml
config:
  web-infra:environment: dev
  web-infra:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAJ...        # set via: pulumi config set --secret dbPassword
```

## Pulumi.prod.yaml

```yaml
config:
  web-infra:environment: prod
  web-infra:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAJ...
```

## Usage

```bash
pulumi stack init dev
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword
pulumi up                        # deploy dev

pulumi stack init prod
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword
pulumi up                        # deploy prod (isolated state)
```

**Notes on acceptance criteria coverage:**
- ✅ Bucket: versioning, AES-256 SSE, public access block
- ✅ RDS: deletion protection, 7-day backups, not public, encrypted on prod
- ✅ Secret: `ConfigSecret` — ciphertext-only in Git
- ✅ IAM: no wildcards; resource-scoped actions; OIDC trust on prod
- ✅ Env isolation: separate Pulumi stacks/configs; changing prod never touches dev state
